<<<
Well, perhaps it is better to air one’s knowledge than ‘one’s ignorance of them; but the escape from both is to be found in evading the pronoun (another cosmopolitan, or also a cosmopolitan) or sacrificing the apposition (& he:was a sentry).
===
Well, perhaps it is better to air one's knowledge than one's ignorance of them; but the escape from both is to be found in evading the pronoun (*another cosmopolitan*, or *also a cosmopolitan*) or sacrificing the apposition (*& he was a sentry*).
>>>

